Fixed all three findings:

- Normalized the discovery root before `symlink_metadata` so a trailing-separator symlink is refused, with a new trailing-slash test (`src/testing/mod.rs:112`, `tests/discovery_test.rs:1465`).
- Split the zero-run message: all-skipped suites now report `No tests were run ... (N skipped)` (`src/lib.rs:165`).
- Benchmark failures are now recorded and reported instead of swallowed, with an end-to-end test (`src/testing/harness.rs:194`, `tests/discovery_test.rs:1407`).

All four gates pass: `cargo fmt --all -- --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test --all-targets` (2955 passed), and `./rbops/verify.sh phase-076`.
